# Case Study: Manufacturing Cloud Migration — Overview

## Quick Facts
- **Client**: Global automotive parts manufacturer, $1.8B revenue, 12 plants
- **Engagement**: 24 weeks, $485K, 8-person team
- **Completion**: August 2025
- **Status**: Successfully completed

## Problem
15-year-old data center infrastructure couldn't scale for IoT predictive maintenance initiative. Aging hardware with 23% annual maintenance growth, 48-hour DR recovery time, 2-week environment provisioning.

## Solution
"Plant-to-Cloud" migration using Azure with:
- Hub-spoke network topology with landing zones
- AKS for containerized workloads
- Kafka real-time data pipeline for shop-floor data
- Terraform/Azure DevOps for IaC
- Azure SQL Managed Instance for database estate
- Power BI for plant-level analytics

## Results
| Metric | Before | After |
|--------|--------|-------|
| Infrastructure Cost | $2.1M/year | $1.2M/year (-42%) |
| Uptime | 99.2% | 99.97% |
| Deployments | Monthly | Daily (12x) |
| DR Recovery | 48 hours | 15 minutes |
| Env. Provisioning | 2 weeks | 30 minutes |

## Key Differentiators Demonstrated
- OT/IT convergence expertise (zero-downtime migration)
- Manufacturing domain knowledge (MES integration)
- Cost optimization (Reserved Instances, right-sizing)

## Technologies
Azure, AKS, Terraform, Azure DevOps, PostgreSQL, Apache Kafka, Power BI

## Relevance
Primary reference for manufacturing cloud migration proposals. Strong outcome metrics and client testimonial.
